ALVA — CPU Intelligence Evolution & Humanization Update

Mission

Perform a major, carefully controlled evolution of CPU Intelligence in the Alva repository.

Repository: hiyroscript/alva

This update has two equally important objectives:

1. Make CPUs substantially more human-like and appropriately balanced across all four difficulties, especially Easy.
2. Make CPUs more genuinely intelligent—not simply better at attacking, but better at understanding the entire match, choosing meaningful objectives, adapting their playstyle, positioning, surviving, and knowing when fighting is or is not the correct decision.

These objectives must coexist.

A smarter CPU must not automatically become a stronger or more frustrating CPU.

An Easy CPU should be capable of making intelligent decisions while still playing like a casual, inexperienced human. Brutal should demonstrate much deeper strategic understanding and better execution, but even Brutal must remain believable as a human-like opponent rather than an omniscient machine.

The single most important design principle is that CPUs must feel human.

I really like the existing CPU Intelligence system. Preserve its architecture, sophistication, universality, and existing features wherever possible.

This is an evolution, not a replacement.

The scope is large. Approach it as a serious AI systems update, with careful investigation, incremental implementation, extensive testing, performance evaluation, and balancing.

