* Time spent intentionally waiting
* Time spent retreating
* Whether waiting actually achieves its objective

Do not use win rate alone as a measure of intelligence.

A CPU that wins more matches but feels robotic has not achieved this update’s goals.

Likewise, a CPU that becomes easy to beat only because it randomly stands still has failed.

The benchmark should reflect realistic performance differences between difficulty levels.

Do not preserve previous high win rates as a requirement when those rates conflict with the new balancing objective.

