PART X — IMPLEMENTATION PROCESS

39. Make the Update in Controlled Phases

This is a large update and must be approached carefully.

Phase 1 — Audit and baseline

Understand the existing architecture, record baseline test and benchmark results, and identify conflicting assumptions.

Phase 2 — Purposeful humanization

Implement justified waiting, improved neutral pacing, and intentional inactivity without compromising liveness or emergency reactions.

Phase 3 — Strategic awareness

Improve understanding of match stakes, long-term objectives, Launch Point recovery, disengagement, and risk-versus-reward.

Phase 4 — Positioning and stage intelligence

Improve destination evaluation, stage control, launch positioning, survival spaces, platform decisions, and hazard awareness.

Phase 5 — Strategy integration

Make strategic objectives influence tactical actions consistently, with appropriate hysteresis and interruption behavior.

Phase 6 — Difficulty rebalance

Tune the actual decision-making and execution differences across Easy, Medium, Hard, and Brutal.

Focus heavily on Easy.

Phase 7 — Testing and refinement

Run relevant tests and benchmarks, investigate regressions, examine behavioral traces, and refine outcomes.

Phase 8 — Documentation

Update the relevant product specification, AI documentation, tests, and player-facing difficulty descriptions in both supported languages if their meaning has changed.

Document the new behaviors and where to tune them.

Keep the repository’s established documentation conventions.

Each phase must preserve working behavior from earlier phases.

Do not make an enormous unvalidated rewrite.

40. Add Explainable Strategic Telemetry

The existing telemetry is valuable.

Expand it where needed to expose:

* Current strategic objective
* Why that objective was selected
* Why the CPU changed objectives
* Whether it is trying to win an exchange or protect the match outcome
* Why it is retreating
* Why it is waiting
* Target destination and positional purpose
* Estimated danger
* Relevant score and clock context
* Both Launch Points
* Whether the last plan succeeded, expired, or failed

Keep the normal execution path efficient.

This information should make it possible to understand CPU behavior without guessing.

If the CPU stands still for several seconds, the debug trace should explain the decision.

If it abandons a recovery strategy and starts attacking, the trace should explain what changed.

